// MULTIPLE deep-path constraints in one predicate, each correlated to a
// request-context value (no free variables). A Read is permitted only if
// there was formerly a Login whose session `id` AND `region` both match the
// current request's — i.e. same session in the same region.
//
//   Login::request{ __drupe.session.id:     context.__drupe.session.id,
//                   __drupe.session.region: context.__drupe.session.region }
//
// Exercises two depth-3 constraints conjoined on one event, both bound to
// the request's own deep fields.
//
// Positive/negative control across two traces:
//   trace_1: prior Login matches the Read on both id and region → permitted.
//   trace_2: IDENTICAL except the prior Login's region differs → the second
//            deep constraint fails → NOT permitted (proves both constraints
//            are enforced, not just the id).

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{
        __drupe.session.id:     context.__drupe.session.id,
        __drupe.session.region: context.__drupe.session.region
    }
};
